  "report": "The updated evidence supports reported Super Saturated (SS) hydration across three credited retailer-review origins, with materially different texture experiences. The supplied input does not identify initial-stage membership or provide a separate initial-stage record, so an initial diagnosis or exact stage-to-stage change cannot be reconstructed reliably. The diagnosis below covers all 11 supplied focal accounts.\n\nSS hydration: A04, A08 and A13 independently report hydration, all as retailer reviews; this is independently repeated reported experience, not cross-venue corroboration or measured efficacy. A04 describes lightweight, refreshing, fast-drying hydration without perceived pore clogging, suitable before makeup. A08 reports hydration while pairing SS with tretinoin and other actives, not an isolated-product test. A13 describes retention through a 12-hour shift, plumpness, less irritation/reactivity and perceived oil reduction with oily-T-zone/dry-sensitive-cheek skin and mild rosacea. Only A13 establishes those particular duration and skin-change details. No direct SS hydration opposition appears in the available text, but A07's body is unavailable. A09 separately reports Avant Guard retaining hydration from SS: one joint-use observation, without separable allocation or evidence of incremental efficacy versus SS alone.\n\nSS texture: A04's lightweight/fast-drying experience contrasts with A13's sticky, shiny, slick finish. A13 describes amount-dependent daytime acceptability and suggests night use for most people; that generalization is the reviewer's, not an established population finding. A03 reports SS is stickier than Wave while continuing SS use because of its presumed higher glycerin content. This supplies another visible actor's first-hand sticky-texture report, but its independence posture is unavailable; cross-venue independent corroboration is therefore not established. The precise Wave-versus-SS comparison has only one first-hand source. A17's thinner-Wave comparison is explicitly speculative: they have never tried Experiment because it does not ship to their location. Generic interest in hydrating serums and ingredient percentages cannot establish SS hydration or texture. Texture conflict is mixed; dose, routine, skin and unknown formulas may matter, but the evidence does not resolve the difference.\n\nOther-product boundaries: A10's overnight retention/glow and A14's silky jelly-to-oil texture and soothing outcomes concern Buffer Jelly, not SS. A14 used a gifted product twice, mixed into moisturizer; after-dermaplaning benefit is anticipated. A15 praises Plasma Wash's silky texture while reporting poor cleansing, severe eye burning and dryness, especially after two washes. This opposes A04's positive cleanser experience, not SS hydration. A18's exceptional Wave hydration and C.R.E.A.M moisture-retention/pilling complaints likewise do not establish SS performance. A17 offers related C.R.E.A.M experience and agreement about needing another layer, not agreement about SS.\n\nBehavior: A04 narrates ordering SS after introduction through a sister, buying Buffer Jelly to seek greater nighttime hydration/repair, then buying the face wash and mesh moisturizer. The account bundles multiple benefits and brand affection; it does not isolate hydration as the cause of every purchase. Its Refill metadata does not independently narrate repurchase. A03 explicitly continues SS despite relative stickiness. A09 deducts a star for mask fit around the nose on a very small head. A13 accommodates stickiness through amount/use timing and advises sticky-averse readers to avoid it; no purchase abandonment is narrated. A14 declares conversion after free receipt, not a paid purchase. A15 considers returning the cleanser but does not report a completed return. Complaint and loyalty coexist; no completed SS repurchase, return or abandonment is established.\n\nEngagement and provenance: All eight focal Junip records have 0 upvotes and 0 downvotes at their supplied observations. Reddit scores are A03=6, A17=7 and A18=10, with observation time unavailable and material_positive=false/not_interpreted. These provide no awarded material resonance and are not verified experiences, independent origins, prevalence or buying effects. Reddit accounts share one thread, and their independence postures are unavailable. Focal counts below count qualifying source accounts, not underlying events. Formula/version is unknown throughout; metadata identifies SS Refill for A04 and First Time for A07/A08 but cannot establish the version used or donate testimony.\n\nMaterial context, outside focal counts: hillary_____k (2025-01-16, score 24) reports buying Regimen Lab Level Serum at Black Friday, brighter/even skin and definite future repurchase intention—not completed repurchase or SS evidence. Skin_Fanatic (2025-01-17, score 2) asks about C.R.E.A.M alternatives while considering trying it; this is interest, not use. Their engagement observation times and independence are unavailable. The shared post asks about Regimen Lab after Instagram advertising; its author, date and engagement are unavailable. Context_f05862db0ee1dcb8c8c6 repeats A18 exactly and adds no source or origin. Product-page and review metadata resolve product references only. A14's explicit free-product disclosure remains material despite rewarded=false metadata.",
